# The build context. Every byte here is uploaded to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs, so a pattern that misses is a slow build rather than a wrong
# one -- except for `target/`, which is both large and actively harmful: without
# this line a local build sends several gigabytes of host build output into the
# image, where `COPY . .` overwrites the cache cargo-chef just built.

# Build output. The largest thing here by an order of magnitude, and the one
# whose absence the `builder` stage depends on: it copies the cooked `target`
# from the `chef` stage and then copies the source over it.
target/
**/target/

# The fetched frontend assets. The Dockerfile fetches them itself, with a retry,
# into the layer that needs them. Copying a local `public/assets/` in would put
# a half-downloaded tree into an image that then builds successfully against it.
apps/lotus-explore-rs/public/assets/ketcher/
apps/lotus-explore-rs/public/assets/vendor/
crates/lotus-web-assets/public/

# Version control and the build context's own metadata. `.git` is not just
# large: the deploy workflow builds from a checkout, and copying `.git` in would
# put the full history -- and every object a shallow clone left out -- into a
# layer the runtime image does not need.
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
.gitignore

# Editor and OS state. `.DS_Store` in particular is copied into the bundle by a
# local `dx build`, and `deploy.yml` has a step to delete it from the export;
# excluding it here is the version of that fix that costs nothing.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Documentation and generated site output. None of it is an input to any stage,
# and the developer docs are in the repository rather than in the image.
docs/
target/doc/
*.md
!README.md
!crates/*/README.md
!apps/*/README.md

# Local agent and knowledge-graph tooling. Not source, and the graph is
# regenerated on demand.
.opencode/
graphify-out/
.code-review-graph/
.mcp.json
AGENTS.md

# Mutation testing output: a report about one run, not an input to anything.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
repro.rs

# Local caches and the coverage report.
.llvm-cov/
lcov.info
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Editorconfig, hook configs and task files. The Dockerfile runs its own
# commands; a hook configuration is a developer's machine, not an input.
.editorconfig
prek.toml
Makefile.toml
make/
.mutable-version

# Secrets. Nothing in this repository needs one at build time, so anything
# matching these patterns is an accident, and an accident that reaches a build
# context is an accident that reaches an image layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Editor swap and backup files.
*~
*.orig
*.rej
